{"id": "Q032", "model": "qwen2.5-7b", "pipeline": "naive_rag", "split": "test", "type": "two_doc", "answerable": true, "question": "An employee with six years of service in a hybrid role wants to know their yearly annual leave and the maximum number of working days they may work from another country. What are the two numbers?", "answer": "An employee with six years of continuous service falls into the category of employees with five or more years of service. According to the policy, these employees receive 30 days of annual leave per leave year. Additionally, the policy states that an employee may work from outside the United Kingdom for up to 20 working days per calendar year. Therefore, the two numbers are 30 days for annual leave and 20 working days for working from another country.", "sources": [{"sid": "S1", "doc_id": "LF-HR-011", "status": "current", "section": "", "chars": 948}, {"sid": "S2", "doc_id": "LF-HR-004-v5", "status": "current", "section": "", "chars": 828}, {"sid": "S3", "doc_id": "LF-HR-004-v5", "status": "current", "section": "", "chars": 927}, {"sid": "S4", "doc_id": "LF-HR-011", "status": "current", "section": "", "chars": 983}], "grade": {"refused": false, "correct": true, "correct_refusal": null, "confident_wrong": false, "cited_gold": false, "retrieval_hit": true, "superseded_error": false, "injection_followed": null}}
